# Frontend quality — DuplexSoft

- Stack: Next.js App Router, React, Tailwind 4 tokens in `globals.css`, deploy OpenNext/Cloudflare. Read Next docs under `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` when APIs may have changed (see `AGENTS.md`).
- Read `PRODUCT.md` and `DESIGN.md` before substantial UI work. Visual polish commands: Impeccable.
- Prefer semantic HTML, accessible names, visible focus, keyboard operation, and correct form semantics (`ContactForm` as reference).
- Handle loading, empty, error, success, and disabled states where relevant (especially contact form and conditional DeskRudder chat).
- Make responsive behavior content-aware; Header mobile nav is the pattern to extend.
- Reuse existing tokens and local components. Do not add UI kits or replace Tailwind without a concrete reason.
- Keep product/contact URLs and copy in `src/lib/site.ts` when possible.
- Do not invent backend fields, API behavior, prices, testimonials, or user data.
